---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Run accessibility tests from your terminal or AI agent"
   summary="Install one package for a CLI, TypeScript API, and MCP server that run axe, control VoiceOver or NVDA, and query WCAG coverage. Every interface calls the same runtime and returns structured results."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section class="split panel">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Try it on a local page</p>
            <h2>Scan your first page</h2>
         </div>
         <pre><code>npm install --global a11ied

a1 doctor
a1 axe --url http://localhost:3000 --level AA --json</code></pre>
         <p>Replace the URL with any page your browser can open. The command returns each violation, its impact, the failing HTML, and the affected selector.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Why run doctor?</div>
         <p class="aside-note"><code>a1 doctor</code> reports which browser, screen reader, and recording tools a11ied can use on this machine.</p>
         <p class="aside-note">Use <code>npm install a11ied</code> without <code>--global</code> when you want the TypeScript API inside a project.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">More than a page scan</p>
         <h2>Screen readers, agents, and targeted checks</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-grid feature-command-grid">
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>Hear the focus order</h3>
            <pre><code>a1 sr start --json
a1 sr next --session &lt;sessionId&gt; --json
a1 sr read --session &lt;sessionId&gt; --json</code></pre>
            <p class="support-copy">Drive VoiceOver, NVDA, or the virtual reader and keep the spoken output.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>Give the tools to an agent</h3>
            <pre><code>npx -y a11ied mcp</code></pre>
            <p class="support-copy">Connect the local MCP server so an agent can call WCAG, axe, and screen reader tools.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>Scan for axe violations</h3>
            <pre><code>a1 axe --url http://localhost:3000 --level AA --json</code></pre>
            <p class="support-copy">Return structured violations for the selected WCAG level.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>Check one WCAG criterion</h3>
            <pre><code>a1 wcag coverage 1.1.1 --json</code></pre>
            <p class="support-copy">See whether automation covers the criterion and read the supported testing strategy.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <h3>Inspect what applies</h3>
            <pre><code>a1 inspect applicable --url http://localhost:3000 --json</code></pre>
            <p class="support-copy">Find forms, dialogs, media, and other page signals tied to WCAG criteria.</p>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Practical guides</p>
         <h2>Test the parts developers ship</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/workflows#drive-a-session">Test navigation with a screen reader</a></strong>
            <span>Move through the interface with VoiceOver, NVDA, or the virtual reader and save what it announces.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/agent-workflows">Add accessibility tests to an AI agent</a></strong>
            <span>Connect the MCP server, scan a page, and drive a screen reader from an agent.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/workflows#gather-evidence">Scan a page during development</a></strong>
            <span>Run axe against a local URL and save structured findings for review or CI.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/workflows#check-one-criterion">Test a specific WCAG criterion</a></strong>
            <span>Check the available automation before running the supported test.</span>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Reference</p>
         <h2>Command and data reference</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/driver-usage">Screen reader driver</a></strong><span>Session lifecycle, actions, focus control, and transcripts.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/mcp-usage">MCP tool reference</a></strong><span>Tool inputs, behavior, and read-only resources.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/cli-reference">CLI reference</a></strong><span>Screen reader, axe, WCAG, inspect, and diagnostic commands.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/agent-skill">Agent skill</a></strong><span>Installation, first use, workflow, and safety rules.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/criterion-lookup">Criterion lookup</a> and <a href="/applicability">applicability</a></strong><span>Find a criterion and check whether the page contains relevant signals.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/wcag-data-sources">WCAG data sources</a></strong><span>See which W3C and axe-core data ships with the package.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/recording-sessions">Recording sessions</a></strong><span>Record real VoiceOver or NVDA sessions.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong><a href="/api-reference">API reference</a></strong><span>Import runtime helpers from TypeScript.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>

</DocShell>
